    text: "Every eBay listing is in a category, and each category asks for its own **item specifics** (eBay\ncalls them aspects), such as Brand, Color or Department. Some are required.\n\n- **Category.** When a product is first published, Crossmart uses eBay's top suggestion for its\n  title. You can search for another in the listing editor\n  and choose it.\n- **Item specifics.** Once the listing has a category, the listing editor shows its item\n  specifics, required ones first, with eBay's allowed values. Brand comes from the product's\n  vendor (`Unbranded` without one), and each variant's options (such as Size) are sent as its own\n  specifics.\n\nWhen a required item specific is missing, Crossmart doesn't send the listing. It shows **Needs\ndetails** with the names eBay requires, such as \"eBay requires these item specifics in this\ncategory: Department.\" Fill them in and save; the listing is sent again.",
